        "description": "Resembles weak/unsalted hashing or hardcoded-secret crypto: it builds an HMAC with hashlib.sha256 over a value named 'token' and a 'secret_key', and the function name hash_token plus SHA256 can trip rules for fast/unsalted hashing of credential-like material. It is actually safe for its purpose: this hashes high-entropy server-generated session/API tokens (secrets.token_urlsafe(48)/token_hex), not user passwords (passwords use Argon2 PasswordHasher elsewhere in this file), and it is a keyed HMAC-SHA256 using _settings.secret_key from configuration (not a literal hardcoded here), giving keyed pre-image resistance so a DB leak does not yield usable tokens. The key is loaded from settings rather than inlined at this sink; no fast unsalted password hashing occurs here."
